=== file: README.md ===
# Comment moderation workflow

This project classifies each supplied comment against the supplied published moderation policy. Low-confidence classifications route to a human moderator. Temporary hiding requires a human confirmation, and removal is only requested after the moderator explicitly answers `remove`.

## Integration status

The plan did not provide a platform API specification, endpoint details, or a way for Loom agents to call tools: it lists no agents. Accordingly, `main.loom` declares the four planned connector tools but does not invoke them. `comment_payload_record` and `published_policy_document` must be supplied by an upstream integration that reads the comment and published policy. Human review is prompted by the workflow; it does not send a ReviewQueue webhook.

Likewise, the workflow records moderator approval or an explicit removal choice, but does not itself call TemporaryHide or RemoveComment. Configure and implement those actions in the moderation application before deployment. Do not treat a note in the workflow as an executed platform change.

Configure `PLATFORM_API_SPEC`, `PLATFORM_API_TOKEN`, and `REVIEW_QUEUE_URL` in the environment for the connector declarations. The platform specification and queue endpoint were not supplied with this project.

## Run the tests

Run `weave test main.loom`. The tests script the classifier and human answers; they do not access a platform or send notifications.
